{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"access token access token","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md","fileName":"Access Token.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Access Token","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Web Identity and Access Control]] [[OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer]] [[TLS Authentication and Secure Remote Access]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Identity and Access Control","OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer","TLS Authentication and Secure Remote Access","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"access token access token","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md","fileName":"Access Token.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Access Token","heading":"Access Token","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An access token is a credential a client presents to an API when requesting a protected operation. The React client obtains a token for the configured API and sends it in the authorization header of its fetch request.\n\nThe API validates the token's issuer, audience, signature, and applicable claims before accepting the identity it represents. A token should be requested and used for its intended resource rather than treated as a general user profile.\n\nIn the stock-checker client, a successful resource-owner password request returns an access token that is retained by the application. The HTTP helper sets that token as a bearer credential before calling the protected GET and PUT API operations.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Identity and Access Control","OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer","TLS Authentication and Secure Remote Access","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"access token access token","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Access Token.md","fileName":"Access Token.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Access Token","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n\n[[aspnetcore3andreact.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Identity and Access Control","OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer","TLS Authentication and Secure Remote Access","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}